{"author":{"id":"f4f7e123ea38957901744390924e1710825e6d55b5113472173231f66fb2d926"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795267309,"nonce":"5wkBGzODksGjC3Czpi/SmPlrEBY=","title":"Follow-up from SCREEN default-palette investigation, 21 November 2026.","message":"The current graphics COLOR handler in src/interp.c evaluates foreground/background but, when graphics are active, only calls gfx_set_color(fg). Original GW-BASIC SCREEN 1 instead uses COLOR background,palette; SCREEN 2 rejects COLOR. The OUT 3D9 emulation in src/portio.c also chooses low-intensity palette entries and does not handle intensity bit 4. These pre-existing gaps are separate from the fixed mode-entry and bare-PALETTE defaults.\n\nImplement the original mode-dependent COLOR forms and palette-intensity behaviour from a pinned Microsoft reference, with interpreter/native cases for background changes, palette 0/1 selection, intensity and transitions through SCREEN/PALETTE. Check immediate redraw semantics explicitly; current PALETTE changes appear on the next drawing flush. Keep the article's v0.18.2 outputs as historical release evidence.\n\nPrimary reference: Microsoft GW-BASIC Interpreter User's Reference (1986), COLOR, PALETTE and SCREEN sections, https://ftpmirror.your.org/pub/misc/bitsavers/pdf/microsoft/gw-basic/410130013-320-R01-0686_Microsoft_GW-BASIC_Interpreter_Users_Reference_1986.pdf","files":null}]}